<title>THAILAND: Thai stocks plummet on profit-taking, forex worry.</title>
<headline>Thai stocks plummet on profit-taking, forex worry.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai stocks closed sharply lower on Monday on profit taking and mounting concerns about listed companies' foreign exchange losses following the baht flotation, brokers said.</p>
<p>The SET index closed off 24.06 points at 633.03 on active trade of 10 billion baht. The SET 50 index ended down 1.89 to 47.27.</p>
